        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital admission of your 88-year-old male patient from 25/07/2020 to 26/07/2020. He presented with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, exhibiting significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. He was commenced on supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, and a course of systemic corticosteroids. Blood tests were performed to exclude secondary causes. He responded well to treatment with notable clinical improvement. He is discharged home with optimised inhaler therapy and a short steroid taper. I recommend close follow-up in your practice and would suggest pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
